#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Understanding high availability and disaster recovery for Quantum Compute {#understanding-high-availability-and-disaster-recovery-for-quantum-compute}"
msgstr "Pag-unawa sa high availability at disaster recovery para sa Quantum Compute {#understanding-high-availability-and-disaster-recovery-for-quantum-compute}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "High availability (HA) is the ability for a service to remain operational and accessible in the presence of unexpected failures. Disaster recovery is the process of recovering the service instance to a working state. IBM Quantum Compute Service customers are not responsible for disaster recovery planning or actions.\n"
msgstr "Ang high availability (HA) ay ang kakayahan ng isang serbisyo na manatiling gumagana at naa-access kahit may mga hindi inaasahang pagpalya. Ang disaster recovery naman ay ang proseso ng pagbabalik ng service instance sa isang gumaganang estado. Ang mga customer ng IBM Quantum Compute Service ay hindi responsable sa pagpaplano o pagkilos para sa disaster recovery.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum Compute is a regional service that fulfills the defined [Service Level Objectives (SLO)](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/resiliency?topic=resiliency-slo) with any paid plan. For more information, see the [Service Level Agreement (SLA)](https://www.ibm.com/support/customer/csol/terms/?id=i126-9268&lc=en) for IBM Cloud&reg;. For more information about the available IBM Cloud regions and data centers for Quantum Compute, see [Service and infrastructure availability by location](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/overview?topic=overview-services_region).\n"
msgstr "Ang Quantum Compute ay isang regional na serbisyo na tumutupad sa mga tinukoy na [Service Level Objectives (SLO)](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/resiliency?topic=resiliency-slo) sa anumang bayad na plano. Para sa karagdagang impormasyon, tingnan ang [Service Level Agreement (SLA)](https://www.ibm.com/support/customer/csol/terms/?id=i126-9268&lc=en) para sa IBM Cloud&reg;. Para sa karagdagang impormasyon tungkol sa mga available na rehiyon at data center ng IBM Cloud para sa Quantum Compute, tingnan ang [Service and infrastructure availability by location](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/overview?topic=overview-services_region).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "High availability architecture {#high-availability-architecture}"
msgstr "Arkitektura ng high availability {#high-availability-architecture}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "High availability features {#high-availability-features}"
msgstr "Mga tampok ng high availability {#high-availability-features}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This service is provisioned across three zones in a multi-zone region with no single point of failure. API requests are routed through a load balancer to the HA instance nodes, each in a different zone.\n"
msgstr "Ang serbisyong ito ay ini-provision sa tatlong zone sa isang multi-zone na rehiyon na walang single point of failure. Ang mga API request ay ini-route sa pamamagitan ng load balancer papunta sa mga HA instance node, na bawat isa ay nasa iba't ibang zone.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If an HA instance node or zone fails, the service continues to run API requests through to the surviving HA instance nodes.  No noticeable degradation of service occurs during a zonal failure.\n"
msgstr "Kung mabigo ang isang HA instance node o zone, patuloy pa ring ipinapadaan ng serbisyo ang mga API request sa mga natitirang HA instance node. Walang kapansin-pansing pagbaba ng kalidad ng serbisyo ang nagaganap sa panahon ng zonal failure.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is available in the following regions:\n"
msgstr "Available ito sa mga sumusunod na rehiyon:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Washington DC (us-east)\n"
msgstr "Washington DC (us-east)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Frankfurt (eu-de)\n"
msgstr "Frankfurt (eu-de)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Disaster recovery {#disaster-recovery}"
msgstr "Disaster recovery {#disaster-recovery}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Disaster recovery (DR) covers the steps required to restore IBM Quantum Compute Service to a working state after a regional failure or other major incident.\n"
msgstr "Sakop ng disaster recovery (DR) ang mga hakbang na kailangan para maibalik sa maayos na estado ang IBM Quantum Compute Service pagkatapos ng regional failure o ibang malaking insidente.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM responsibilities {#ibm-responsibilities}"
msgstr "Mga responsibilidad ng IBM {#ibm-responsibilities}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM is responsible for the following disaster recovery tasks:\n"
msgstr "Responsable ang IBM sa mga sumusunod na gawain sa disaster recovery:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Restoring or rebuilding the provisioning environments and resources in the affected region.\n"
msgstr "Pagpapanumbalik o muling pagbuo ng mga provisioning environment at resource sa apektadong rehiyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Automatically recovering and restoring IBM Quantum Compute Service capabilities to normal operations following a regional or major incident.\n"
msgstr "Awtomatikong pagbawi at pagpapanumbalik ng mga kakayahan ng IBM Quantum Compute Service sa normal na operasyon kasunod ng regional o malaking insidente.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Your responsibilities {#your-responsibilities}"
msgstr "Mga responsibilidad mo {#your-responsibilities}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If a regional failure occurs, IBM recommends the following course of action.\n"
msgstr "Kung magkaroon ng regional failure, inirerekomenda ng IBM ang sumusunod na hakbang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Switch to an alternate region (recommended)**\n"
msgstr "**Lumipat sa alternatibong rehiyon (inirerekomenda)**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If your workload allows it, provision a new IBM Quantum Compute Service [instance](/guides/instances) in the alternate region and resubmit any impacted jobs there. This is the fastest path to resuming operations.\n"
msgstr "Kung pinapayagan ito ng iyong workload, mag-provision ng bagong [instance](/guides/instances) ng IBM Quantum Compute Service sa alternatibong rehiyon at isumite muli roon ang mga naapektuhang job. Ito ang pinakamabilis na paraan para ipagpatuloy ang operasyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You might not be able to switch regions if, for example:\n"
msgstr "Maaaring hindi ka makalipat ng rehiyon kung, halimbawa:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Your work requires specific qubit characteristics that are only available in the affected region.\n"
msgstr "Nangangailangan ang trabaho mo ng mga partikular na katangian ng qubit na available lang sa apektadong rehiyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Regulatory or data-residency requirements prevent you from using a different region.\n"
msgstr "Pinipigilan ka ng mga regulatory o data-residency requirement na gumamit ng ibang rehiyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Wait for service recovery in your region**\n"
msgstr "**Hintayin ang pagbawi ng serbisyo sa iyong rehiyon**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If switching regions is not an option, wait for IBM to recover the service in your region. IBM will communicate status and progress through the [IBM Cloud status page](https://cloud.ibm.com/status). After recovery is confirmed, resubmit any impacted jobs.\n"
msgstr "Kung hindi opsyon ang paglipat ng rehiyon, hintayin na maibalik ng IBM ang serbisyo sa iyong rehiyon. Ipapaalam ng IBM ang status at progress sa pamamagitan ng [IBM Cloud status page](https://cloud.ibm.com/status). Kapag nakumpirma na ang pagbawi, isumite muli ang mga naapektuhang job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Additional responsibilities {#additional-responsibilities}"
msgstr "Karagdagang mga responsibilidad {#additional-responsibilities}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a full breakdown of IBM and customer responsibilities during a disaster recovery event, see [Disaster recovery](/guides/responsibilities#disaster-recovery) in the Responsibilities topic.\n"
msgstr "Para sa buong paghahati ng mga responsibilidad ng IBM at ng customer sa panahon ng disaster recovery event, tingnan ang [Disaster recovery](/guides/responsibilities#disaster-recovery) sa paksang Responsibilities.\n"
